            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="1298" n="1193" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v03mSupp/pg1193"/>

                <head>282. Briefing Note for the December 20 NSC
                        Meeting<anchor n="1" xml:id="d282-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-12-19">December 19,
                        1960</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d282-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d282-1"/>
                <p>The first part of the [illegible in the original] item is a report by NASA on its outer space programs.</p>
                <p>At the meeting on November 7, 1960, the Council heard a presentation by
                    [illegible in the original] on the outer space programs being <pb facs="1299"
                        n="1194" type="typeset" xml:id="pg1194"/> conducted under Defense auspices,
                    [illegible in the original] that meeting that the President requested NASA to present to the Council a report (a) on
                    the outer space programs now being conducted under the auspices of NASA, and (b) on the level of effort the United
                    States should devote to non-military outer space activities in the future.</p>
                <p>(CALL ON: DR. [illegible in the original])</p>
                <p>The second part of the first item is a presentation by Dr. Kistiakowsky of a report by the Science
                    Advisory Committee on “Man in Space.”</p>
                <p>(CALL ON: DR. KISTIAKOWSKY)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
